  "what": "new Fig. 9 with three slabs (b midway between the first and the last prefrontal entry, c rule B, d the present slab), counted on the labels of record (all bundle classes); the drawing is the labels without the light class; figures not adopted",
  "rules": "Shared definitions (as the distance plot of the bundles along the capsule, and the present slab's record, fig_tracer_v11_h9_s11wr17 b.*):\n  charted voxels = <S>_Bundles_mri-template_sections_footprint >= 0.1 (the labels' charted sections in the template), MF191 mirrored onto the right;\n  capsule = SARM level 6 label 50, right side (x > 0); window = the capsule dilated by 8 voxels (2 mm), right side, in the brain mask;\n  slab = three consecutive template planes (0.25 mm each, 0.75 mm), named by its center plane;\n  the section of a voxel = the section of its nearest section-index voxel (<S>_section_index_mri-template, MF191 mirrored).\n\nRule B (the rostral slab, b): per case and slab, count the charted voxels inside the capsule (not dilated). A case has entered the\ncapsule at a slab when it has >= 20 there (the distance plot's own minimum per point). A case's entry = its most rostral such slab.\nb = the most rostral slab at which all three prefrontal cases (MM1, MM3, MF8) have entered, i.e. the most caudal of their three entry\nslabs; it must lie rostral of MM2's entry. The present slab's rule (c), from the record: three consecutive planes; the largest minimum\nover the four cases of charted in-capsule voxels; ties nearest 18.0 mm.\nAlternative three-slab version: b as above; c = MM2's entry slab; d = the most caudal slab anywhere caudal of c (not necessarily\ncontiguous with it) at which all four cases have >= 20.",
